{
  "id": "source-monitoring",
  "term": "source monitoring",
  "definition": "Source monitoring is the mental process of judging where a memory, thought, or other mental experience came from. When it fails, a person may confuse imagined events with real ones or mix directly perceived information with suggestions, heard information, or prior knowledge.",
